From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 20:26:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Let a section's counts answer the two box scans inside
 Entity.move

Entity.move asks two questions of an entity's whole bounding box on every
tick, and for a mob standing in a field the answer to both is no:

  isFlammableWithin walks the box looking for fire or lava - 2.24% of the
    server thread under the saturating bench
  checkBlockCollisions walks it looking for a block that reacts to an entity
    standing in it - 3.27%, and it had to read each block to find out, since
    hasEntityCollisionHandler is a property of the block

ChunkSection has counted the water and lava blocks it holds since patch 0220.
It now also counts fire, and the blocks with an entity collision handler -
that predicate is a constant per block class, every override returns a literal,
so it can be tallied exactly like a material. mayHoldLiquid becomes a mask over
a shared walk, and the two callers above get their own guards.

Where the counters say no, neither scan reads a single block. Anything the
counters cannot answer - an unloaded chunk, decoration in flight - answers yes
and the caller scans exactly as before.

The counters are load-bearing in one direction: one that drifts below the truth
would silently stop an entity noticing it is standing in fire or on a pressure
plate. ChunkSectionBlockCountTest, widened from the liquid one, walks a section
through twenty thousand random writes over a palette that provably covers every
counted kind, and the audit under debugVerifyAthenaIndexes now recounts all
four.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

